jistanidiot@gmail.com wrote:

> I've been trying to figure out the best symbol to use for a boulder.
> So far I know I don't like the ' character used as the default.  I'd
> like to use 0 but that looks too much like O.

Use a 0, but choose a different font or font size. In Courier, for
example, the difference between O and 0 is AFAICT 0 at small point
sizes, but more noticable at larger size; in Lucida Console, the
situation is similar; in OCR A (which would perhaps be less than ideally
readable otherwise), the O is a diamond while the 0 is a square; in
Bitstream Sans Mono, the 0 has a dot in the centre, which the O does
not; and in many system fonts, the 0 has a slash and the O doesn't.

